Elf rangers get a +2 hit bonus, a +1 damage bonus, and a +1 possible
extra shot per turn -- when they use elven arrows from an elven bow.
Note that although Orc rangers can get a similiar +1 possible extra
shot per turn, they never get the +hit bonus or the +damage bonus that
the elven rangers get... AND the orc arrows naturally do less damage
than the elf arrows.

Also, I'd rather have an elven cloak than a cloak of displacement,
since the elven cloak is MC3, and the cloak of displacement is only
MC2.  The special ability of the cloak of displacement doesn't always
work, and I'd rather play the game safely, than cross my fingers and
hope the cloak of displacement will work.  Additionally, I'd rather
not have displacement, because I'd rather the enemies try to line
themselves up in a row when they chase me, so that I can more easily
fill them all full of arrows.


